From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivela=CC=88?= <vkivela@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:12:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] extensions: offer the scripting namespace

Bitwarden asks the browser to inject its autofill content script through
chrome.scripting.executeScript, which QtWebEngine did not offer, so a
password manager could reach a page's forms only through the content
scripts declared in its manifest.

Chrome's scripting_api compiles unchanged once its own two includes point
at QtWebEngine's copies of the schema and header: it resolves a tab through
ExtensionsBrowserClient::IsValidTabId and GetScriptExecutorForTab, which
the tab registry now answers with a ScriptExecutor owned by the tab's
WebContents.

